IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mc15-nouns`
IMPORT `mc15-ch60-63`

-- Tests for chapters 60 to 63.  Every expected value was written from the text before the file
-- was run; unit ids (61.4, 61.14 ...) are those of the coverage table in NOTES.md.  The dates in
-- Exception: the assertions marked `-- RECONCILED` were re-derived after a first run, each from the text and the rule, and each comment quotes the original:
-- in the first pass those that expected a no where the text does not say no in its own words, and in the second pass (2026-10-30) those that expected "not covered"
-- where the text's own "if", "while", "until", "unless" or "except" makes the no (NOTES.md, "Where the text says no, and where it does not").
-- chapter 61 are arbitrary; the text names no calendar and no year.

§ `Tests -- chapters 60 to 63`

§§ `Chapter 60 -- the observance of the customs and liberties by all`

-- Arguments are the person is of the kingdom, clergy or lay; the person has men.
#ASSERT `ch 60 -- the person must observe the customs and liberties towards his men` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 60 -- the person must observe the customs and liberties towards his men` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 60 -- the person must observe the customs and liberties towards his men` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
-- expect: MUST `observe towards his men the customs and liberties which the King has granted towards his men`
#TRACE `ch 60 -- the customs and liberties shall be observed by all of our kingdom towards their men` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 60 -- the customs and liberties shall be observed by all of our kingdom towards their men` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a member of the kingdom, clergy or lay` DOES `observe towards his men the customs and liberties which the King has granted towards his men` AT 6
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 60 -- the customs and liberties shall be observed by all of our kingdom towards their men` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100

§§ `Chapter 61 -- the security of the five-and-twenty barons`

-- 61.2: a permission, not a duty.
-- expect: MAY `choose five-and-twenty barons of the kingdom, whomsoever they will`
#TRACE `ch 61 -- the barons choose five-and-twenty barons of the kingdom, whomsoever they will` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 61 -- the barons choose five-and-twenty barons of the kingdom, whomsoever they will` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the barons` DOES `choose five-and-twenty barons of the kingdom, whomsoever they will` AT 6
-- 61.3:
-- expect: MUST `observe and hold, and cause to be observed, the peace and liberties granted and confirmed by the Charter`
#TRACE `ch 61 -- the five-and-twenty barons shall be bound to observe and hold, and cause to be observed, the peace and liberties` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 61 -- the five-and-twenty barons shall be bound to observe and hold, and cause to be observed, the peace and liberties` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the five-and-twenty barons` DOES `observe and hold, and cause to be observed, the peace and liberties granted and confirmed by the Charter` AT 6
-- 61.4: arguments are the King, his justiciar, his bailiffs or an officer has been at fault or has broken an article; the offence has been notified to four barons of the five-and-twenty.
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the four barons are to repair to the King and petition for the transgression to be corrected` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Obliged
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30: was "#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the four barons are to repair to the King and petition for the transgression to be corrected` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`"; now the text's no, because "and the offence be notified to four barons" is a limb of the text's own if, and fewer than four were told (F61i).
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the four barons are to repair to the King and petition for the transgression to be corrected` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Not obliged`
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30: was "#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the four barons are to repair to the King and petition for the transgression to be corrected` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`"; now the text's no, because "if we ... shall in anything be at fault" is the other limb of the same if, and there was no fault.
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the four barons are to repair to the King and petition for the transgression to be corrected` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not obliged`
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- to whom the four barons repair` FALSE EQUALS `the King`
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- to whom the four barons repair` TRUE EQUALS `the King's chief justiciar`
-- expect: MUST `repair to the King, or to his justiciar if he is out of the realm, and, laying the transgression before him, petition to have it corrected without delay`
#TRACE `ch 61 -- the said four barons shall repair to us and petition to have that transgression corrected without delay` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 61 -- the said four barons shall repair to us and petition to have that transgression corrected without delay` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `four of the five-and-twenty barons` DOES `repair to the King, or to his justiciar if he is out of the realm, and, laying the transgression before him, petition to have it corrected without delay` AT 6
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 61 -- the said four barons shall repair to us and petition to have that transgression corrected without delay` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- 61.5 and 61.6: 15 January 2001 plus forty days is 24 February 2001; 25 December 2001 plus forty days is 3 February 2002.
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the last day for correcting the transgression` (Date 15 1 2001) EQUALS Date 24 2 2001
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the last day for correcting the transgression` (Date 25 12 2001) EQUALS Date 3 2 2002
-- Arguments are the day it was intimated, the day in question, the transgression was corrected within the forty days.
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the four barons are to refer the matter to the rest of the five-and-twenty` (Date 15 1 2001) (Date 24 2 2001) FALSE EQUALS `Not obliged`
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the four barons are to refer the matter to the rest of the five-and-twenty` (Date 15 1 2001) (Date 25 2 2001) FALSE EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the four barons are to refer the matter to the rest of the five-and-twenty` (Date 15 1 2001) (Date 25 2 2001) TRUE EQUALS `Not obliged`
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the four barons are to refer the matter to the rest of the five-and-twenty` (Date 15 1 2001) (Date 15 1 2001) FALSE EQUALS `Not obliged`
-- expect: MUST `refer the matter to the rest of the five-and-twenty barons`
#TRACE `ch 61 -- the four barons aforesaid shall refer that matter to the rest of the five-and-twenty barons` (Date 15 1 2001) (Date 25 2 2001) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 61 -- the four barons aforesaid shall refer that matter to the rest of the five-and-twenty barons` (Date 15 1 2001) (Date 25 2 2001) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `four of the five-and-twenty barons` DOES `refer the matter to the rest of the five-and-twenty barons` AT 6
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 61 -- the four barons aforesaid shall refer that matter to the rest of the five-and-twenty barons` (Date 15 1 2001) (Date 25 2 2001) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 61 -- the four barons aforesaid shall refer that matter to the rest of the five-and-twenty barons` (Date 15 1 2001) (Date 24 2 2001) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- 61.7: arguments are the matter has been referred to the five-and-twenty barons, redress has been obtained as they deem fit.
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the five-and-twenty barons are to distrain and distress the King` TRUE FALSE EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the five-and-twenty barons are to distrain and distress the King` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not obliged`
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the five-and-twenty barons are to distrain and distress the King` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
-- expect: MUST `distrain and distress the King in all possible ways, together with the community of the whole land, by seizing his castles, lands and possessions and in any other way they can`
#TRACE `ch 61 -- those five-and-twenty barons shall, together with the community of the whole land, distrain and distress us in all possible ways` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 61 -- those five-and-twenty barons shall, together with the community of the whole land, distrain and distress us in all possible ways` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the five-and-twenty barons` DOES `distrain and distress the King in all possible ways, together with the community of the whole land, by seizing his castles, lands and possessions and in any other way they can` AT 6
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 61 -- those five-and-twenty barons shall, together with the community of the whole land, distrain and distress us in all possible ways` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- 61.8:
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the person may be harmed in the distraint` `the King's own person` EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the person may be harmed in the distraint` `the person of the queen` EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the person may be harmed in the distraint` `the person of a child of the King` EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the person may be harmed in the distraint` `someone else` EQUALS `Bar not covered`
-- expect: MUST NOT `harm the person of the King, of the queen or of their children in distraining and distressing the King`
#TRACE `ch 61 -- saving harmless our own person, and the persons of our queen and children` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 61 -- saving harmless our own person, and the persons of our queen and children` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the five-and-twenty barons` DOES `harm the person of the King, of the queen or of their children in distraining and distressing the King` AT 6
-- 61.9:
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the five-and-twenty barons are to resume their old relations towards the King` TRUE EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the five-and-twenty barons are to resume their old relations towards the King` FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
-- expect: MUST `resume their old relations towards the King`
#TRACE `ch 61 -- when redress has been obtained, they shall resume their old relations towards us` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 61 -- when redress has been obtained, they shall resume their old relations towards us` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the five-and-twenty barons` DOES `resume their old relations towards the King` AT 6
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 61 -- when redress has been obtained, they shall resume their old relations towards us` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- 61.10:
-- expect: MAY `swear to obey the orders of the five-and-twenty barons for the execution of the aforesaid matters and, along with them, molest the King to the utmost of his power`
#TRACE `ch 61 -- let whoever in the country desires it swear to obey the orders of the said five-and-twenty barons` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 61 -- let whoever in the country desires it swear to obey the orders of the said five-and-twenty barons` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `whoever in the country desires it` DOES `swear to obey the orders of the five-and-twenty barons for the execution of the aforesaid matters and, along with them, molest the King to the utmost of his power` AT 6
-- 61.11:
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the person has the King's leave to swear` TRUE EQUALS Entitled
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the person has the King's leave to swear` FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
-- expect: MUST NOT `forbid anyone to swear to obey the orders of the five-and-twenty barons`
#TRACE `ch 61 -- we shall never forbid anyone to swear` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 61 -- we shall never forbid anyone to swear` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `forbid anyone to swear to obey the orders of the five-and-twenty barons` AT 6
-- 61.12: arguments are the person is in the land, of himself and of his own accord he is unwilling to swear.
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the person is to be compelled by the King's command to swear` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the person is to be compelled by the King's command to swear` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the person is to be compelled by the King's command to swear` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
-- expect: MUST `compel by his command those in the land who of themselves and of their own accord are unwilling to swear to the twenty-five, to swear to that effect`
#TRACE `ch 61 -- we shall by our command compel the same to swear to the effect foresaid` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 61 -- we shall by our command compel the same to swear to the effect foresaid` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `compel by his command those in the land who of themselves and of their own accord are unwilling to swear to the twenty-five, to swear to that effect` AT 6
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 61 -- we shall by our command compel the same to swear to the effect foresaid` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- 61.13:
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- another baron is to be chosen in his place` TRUE EQUALS Obliged
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30 (sweep of the NOT-COVERED branches): was "#ASSERT `ch 61 -- another baron is to be chosen in his place` FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`"; the text's own word on that branch makes the no (see the FALSE-kind comment in the module).
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- another baron is to be chosen in his place` FALSE EQUALS `Not obliged`
-- expect: MUST `choose another baron in his place according to their own judgment`
#TRACE `ch 61 -- those of the said twenty-five barons who are left shall choose another in his place according to their own judgment` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: MUST `be sworn in the same way as the others`
#TRACE `ch 61 -- those of the said twenty-five barons who are left shall choose another in his place according to their own judgment` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the barons who are left of the five-and-twenty` DOES `choose another baron in his place according to their own judgment` AT 3
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 61 -- those of the said twenty-five barons who are left shall choose another in his place according to their own judgment` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the barons who are left of the five-and-twenty` DOES `choose another baron in his place according to their own judgment` AT 3
    PARTY `the baron chosen in the place of one of the five-and-twenty` DOES `be sworn in the same way as the others` AT 5
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 61 -- those of the said twenty-five barons who are left shall choose another in his place according to their own judgment` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- 61.14: arguments are the number of the five-and-twenty present, the number of those present who ordain or command it.
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- what those present ordain or command is held as fixed and established` 25 13 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- what those present ordain or command is held as fixed and established` 25 12 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- what those present ordain or command is held as fixed and established` 20 11 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- what those present ordain or command is held as fixed and established` 20 10 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- what those present ordain or command is held as fixed and established` 4 2 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- what those present ordain or command is held as fixed and established` 3 2 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- what those present ordain or command is held as fixed and established` 3 1 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- what those present ordain or command is held as fixed and established` 1 1 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- what those present ordain or command is held as fixed and established` 1 0 EQUALS FALSE
-- 61.15, 61.16 and 61.17:
-- expect: MUST `swear that they will faithfully observe all that is aforesaid, and cause it to be observed with all their might`
#TRACE `ch 61 -- the said twenty-five shall swear that they will faithfully observe all that is aforesaid` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 61 -- the said twenty-five shall swear that they will faithfully observe all that is aforesaid` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the five-and-twenty barons` DOES `swear that they will faithfully observe all that is aforesaid, and cause it to be observed with all their might` AT 6
-- expect: MUST NOT `procure from anyone, directly or indirectly, anything whereby any part of these concessions and liberties might be revoked or diminished`
#TRACE `ch 61 -- we shall procure nothing from anyone, directly or indirectly, whereby any part of these concessions and liberties might be revoked or diminished` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 61 -- we shall procure nothing from anyone, directly or indirectly, whereby any part of these concessions and liberties might be revoked or diminished` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `procure from anyone, directly or indirectly, anything whereby any part of these concessions and liberties might be revoked or diminished` AT 6
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the thing procured` TRUE EQUALS `Void and null`
#ASSERT `ch 61 -- the thing procured` FALSE EQUALS `Validity not covered`
-- expect: MUST NOT `use personally or by another a thing procured to revoke or diminish a part of these concessions and liberties`
#TRACE `ch 61 -- we shall never use it personally or by another` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `ch 61 -- we shall never use it personally or by another` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `use personally or by another a thing procured to revoke or diminish a part of these concessions and liberties` AT 6

§§ `Chapter 62 -- the remission of ill-will and trespasses`

#ASSERT `ch 62 -- the ill-will, hatreds and bitterness are remitted and pardoned` TRUE EQUALS Entitled
#ASSERT `ch 62 -- the ill-will, hatreds and bitterness are remitted and pardoned` FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
-- 62.2: arguments are the trespass was occasioned by the said quarrel, it was committed from Easter in the sixteenth year of the reign till the restoration of peace.
#ASSERT `ch 62 -- the trespass is fully remitted and completely forgiven, as far as pertains to the King` TRUE TRUE EQUALS Entitled
#ASSERT `ch 62 -- the trespass is fully remitted and completely forgiven, as far as pertains to the King` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 62 -- the trespass is fully remitted and completely forgiven, as far as pertains to the King` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`

§§ `Chapter 63 -- the enjoining clause and the oath`

#ASSERT `ch 63 -- the person has and holds all the aforesaid liberties, rights and concessions for himself and his heirs` TRUE EQUALS Entitled
#ASSERT `ch 63 -- the person has and holds all the aforesaid liberties, rights and concessions for himself and his heirs` FALSE EQUALS `Entitlement not covered`
-- expect: MUST `keep all the conditions of the Charter in good faith and without evil intent`
#TRACE `ch 63 -- all these conditions shall be kept in good faith and without evil intent` `the King` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 63 -- all these conditions shall be kept in good faith and without evil intent` `the King` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `keep all the conditions of the Charter in good faith and without evil intent` AT 6
-- expect: MUST `keep all the conditions of the Charter in good faith and without evil intent`
#TRACE `ch 63 -- all these conditions shall be kept in good faith and without evil intent` `the barons` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 63 -- all these conditions shall be kept in good faith and without evil intent` `the barons` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the barons` DOES `keep all the conditions of the Charter in good faith and without evil intent` AT 6
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 63 -- all these conditions shall be kept in good faith and without evil intent` `a bailiff` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100

